WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.610
On 6 August 1945, a nuclear
bomb fell on Hiroshima.

2
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.160
Three days later,
another fell on Nagasaki.

3
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.640
They are still the only times nuclear
weapons have been used in war.

4
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.810
Today the UK keeps
nuclear-armed submarines,

5
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.060
called Trident, hoping never to fire them.

6
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.110
So can owning a weapon you must
never use really keep the world safe?

7
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.490
In this mission, you'll see how
deterrence is meant to work,

8
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.260
and what could go wrong.

9
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:35.450
Then you'll weigh a utilitarian case for
these weapons against religious objections.

10
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: weigh up whether owning
nuclear weapons can be morally justified.
